-Writing `D=N_B-N_A` turns `N_A=p(2r+1)` into `2p^2+(2D+1)p-N_A=0`; one exact integer square root recovers `p`, then `r=p+D`.  The module counts 14 high-level exact operations.  This large compression gap, not computational hardness, is the Track B claim.
